{
 "name": "oculudentavis_specimen",
 "description": "The second 'Oculudentavis' amber specimen (030), facing right: a partial lizard skeleton. Complete domed skull at the right with a huge orbit ringed by bony scleral plates, toothed upper and lower jaws (snout less beaky than oculudentavis_skull), vertebral chain and curved ribs running left, a brown scaly skin patch over the neck/shoulder and a darker soft-tissue patch on the belly, two clawed front legs hanging down, over a faint tan soft-tissue ghost. Cream bone #efe6d0. Anchor centre, ~440x210 (x -216..220, y -106..106). Fits the amber_bead core.",
